      "summaries": {
        "en": "OpenScreen is an open-source screen recording tool that helps developers create polished software demos without subscription fees or watermarks. Built with Electron and PixiJS, it offers real-time visual effects like cursor highlighting and smooth transitions during recording. Users can capture their screen, apply enhancements, and export professional-quality videos for tutorials, product showcases, or documentation, making it ideal for both personal projects and commercial use.",
        "zh": "OpenScreen 是一款开源屏幕录制工具，专为开发者设计，用于制作精美的软件演示视频，无需订阅费或水印。它基于 Electron 和 PixiJS 构建，在录制时实时添加光标高亮和平滑过渡等视觉效果，提升演示的专业度。用户可轻松录制屏幕、应用增强效果，并导出高质量视频，适用于教程制作、产品展示或文档补充，既支持个人项目，也适合商业用途，让技术分享更生动直观。",
        "es": "OpenScreen is an open-source screen recording tool that helps developers create polished software demos without subscription fees or watermarks. Built with Electron and PixiJS, it offers real-time visual effects like cursor highlighting and smooth transitions during recording. Users can capture their screen, apply enhancements, and export professional-quality videos for tutorials, product showcases, or documentation, making it ideal for both personal projects and commercial use.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "openscreen stands out for electron, open-source, and pixijs in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "OpenScreen is an open-source screen recording tool that helps developers create polished software demos without subscription fees or watermarks. Built with Electron and PixiJS, it offers real-time visual effects like cursor highlighting and smooth transitions during recording. Users can capture their screen, apply enhancements, and export professional-quality videos for tutorials, product showcases, or documentation, making it ideal for both personal projects and commercial use.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/siddharthvaddem/openscreen for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
