      "summaries": {
        "en": "Oh My Codex is a TypeScript framework that enhances AI code generation by making it more interactive and collaborative. It introduces modular hooks and agent teams that allow developers to customize how AI models process and generate code, enabling real-time feedback and multi-agent workflows. You can integrate it into existing development environments to create smarter coding assistants, experiment with different agent configurations, or build custom extensions for specific programming tasks.",
        "zh": "Oh My Codex 是一个基于 TypeScript 的框架，旨在提升 AI 代码生成的交互性与协作性。它通过模块化的钩子和智能体团队机制，让开发者能够灵活定制 AI 模型处理代码的方式，支持实时反馈和多智能体协同工作流。该框架的核心在于将代码生成过程分解为可组合的步骤，便于调试和优化。你可以将其集成到现有开发工具中，构建更智能的编程助手，尝试不同的智能体配置来解决复杂编码问题，或扩展自定义功能以适应特定项目需求。",
        "es": "Oh My Codex is a TypeScript framework that enhances AI code generation by making it more interactive and collaborative. It introduces modular hooks and agent teams that allow developers to customize how AI models process and generate code, enabling real-time feedback and multi-agent workflows. You can integrate it into existing development environments to create smarter coding assistants, experiment with different agent configurations, or build custom extensions for specific programming tasks.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "oh-my-codex gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Oh My Codex is a TypeScript framework that enhances AI code generation by making it more interactive and collaborative. It introduces modular hooks and agent teams that allow developers to customize how AI models process and generate code, enabling real-time feedback and multi-agent workflows. You can integrate it into existing development environments to create smarter coding assistants, experiment with different agent configurations, or build custom extensions for specific programming tasks.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/Yeachan-Heo/oh-my-codex for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
